SUMMARY:Deadline: Waging Nonviolence Journalism Fellowship (Fall 2026)
DESCRIPTION:The first Waging Nonviolence Fellowship is a five-month remote 
 journalism programme for writers reporting on social movements\, peace\, j
 ustice and nonviolent action. It is framed as journalistic training: fello
 ws work closely with senior editor Jessica Stites and editor-in-chief Eric
  Stoner and come out with a body of clips on an undercovered movement beat
 . WORK: five monthly feature articles of at least 1\,500 words each for Wa
 ging Nonviolence\, plus an initial meeting and check-ins as needed\; fello
 ws are expected to find their own stories\, hit deadlines and respond prom
 ptly by email. PAY: a $500 stipend up front plus $250 per published story\
 , so $1\,750 across the full run. ELIGIBILITY: US-based\; experience repor
 ting on or analysing social movements\; excellent writing and clean copy\;
  genuine investment in peace and justice organising. Established connectio
 ns to activist groups and communities\, and knowledge of civil resistance 
 history\, theory\, strategy and tactics\, are preferred. APPLICATION: via 
 a Google Form linked from the announcement\; no resume or CV required. Dea
 dline 10 August 2026. Contact: contact@wagingnonviolence.org.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Waging Nonviolence\nLocation: Remote\, with a flexible self-directed 
 schedule. RESTRICTED: US-based writers.\nAward: $500 initial stipend plus 
 $250 per published story\, up to $1\,750 in total. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Five months (Fall 2026)\, remote and self-directed\; five monthly 
 feature articles of at least 1\,500 words each\n\nMore: https://wagingnonv
 iolence.org/2026/07/waging-nonviolence-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://wagingnonviolence.org/2026/07/waging-nonviolence-fellowship/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, with a flexible self-directed schedule. RESTRICTED: US-ba
 sed writers.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:developh-tropical-internet-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260823
SUMMARY:Deadline: Developh Tropical Internet Research Fellowship (Philippin
 es / Southeast Asia)
DESCRIPTION:Developh invites applications for its inaugural Tropical Intern
 et Research Fellowship\, supporting researchers\, writers\, and artist-tec
 hnologists at any career stage who are investigating the cultural and mate
 rial conditions of the internet across the Philippines and Southeast Asia 
 and are interested in producing written work. The fellowship runs seasonal
 ly (every 1-2 years) to support new writing about the 'tropical internet':
  the online as experienced from the tropical regions of the Philippines an
 d broader Southeast Asia\, concerned with heat\, extremes\, monsoons\, dis
 tance\, islandedness\, improvisation\, pluralities\, and diasporas. It nur
 tures work examining how the internet is lived\, built\, resisted\, and fe
 lt across the region\, welcoming research on infrastructures\, digital lab
 or\, rural-urban internet inequities\, algorithmic cultures\, online intim
 acies\, and the entangled relationships between land\, technology\, and th
 e body\, and how colonial\, corporate\, and extractive forces shape infras
 tructures for connection. WHO SHOULD APPLY: researchers\, writers\, design
 ers\, artists\, and technologists with strong ties to the Philippines or b
 roader Southeast Asia\; applicants welcome from any present location\, wit
 h preference to those within the Philippines\, particularly outside Metro 
 Manila. Work may relate to an academic thesis\, but the produced artifact 
 must be a distinct new work separate from the thesis. COMMITMENTS: produce
  an output by January 2027 (suggested minimum ~2000 words\, in English\, F
 ilipino\, or any Philippine language)\; publish with Developh by March-Apr
 il 2027 with editorial and publication support\; present findings by March
 -April 2027\; share citations and research notes for a collective referenc
 e library\; attend three cohort group meetings\; and participate in editor
 ial review and feedback cycles (prototypes and interim essays are encourag
 ed\; a fully finished output is not required). FELLOWS RECEIVE: a PHP 20\,
 000 (~USD 300) stipend\, with a potential additional stipend depending on 
 fieldwork/research needs\; peer learning through online cohort sessions\; 
 check-ins with the Developh team and guest critics\; editorial and publish
 ing support (coding\, design\, hosting)\; and free access to Developh even
 ts and workshops for the fellowship period. TIMELINE: application deadline
  22 August 2026\; writing and research September 2026 to January 2027\; pu
 blication and presentations March 2027 onwards. Apply via the Google Form.
  Free to apply.\n\nOrganisation: Developh\nLocation: Remote / Philippines 
 and broader Southeast Asia. Applicants welcome from any location\; prefere
 nce to those within the Philippines\, particularly outside Metro Manila.\n
 Award: PHP 20\,000 (~USD 300) stipend\, with a potential additional stipen
 d depending on fieldwork/research needs. Plus editorial and publishing sup
 port (coding\, design\, hosting for the final output)\, online cohort sess
 ions\, check-ins with the Developh team and guest critics\, and free acces
 s to Developh events and workshops for the fellowship period. Free to appl
 y.\nDuration: Research and writing September 2026 to January 2027 (5 month
 s)\; publication and presentations March to April 2027 onwards\n\nMore: ht
 tps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSffbGYSmGNCPuFxN_7qUiAUMd9PlA3QtiIg
 5OBUHxBsRyoIpw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSffbGYSmGNCPuFxN_7qUiAUMd9PlA3
 QtiIg5OBUHxBsRyoIpw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / Philippines and broader Southeast Asia. Applicants welcom
 e from any location\; preference to those within the Philippines\, particu
 larly outside Metro Manila.
END:VEVENT
