UID:adina-talve-goodman-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:Deadline: One Story: Adina Talve-Goodman Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Annual educational fellowship honouring the memory of author an
 d former One Story managing editor Adina Talve-Goodman: a year-long mentor
 ship on the craft of fiction writing with One Story magazine\, aimed at gi
 ving a writer outside the fold a significant career boost. WHAT THE FELLOW
  RECEIVES: access to One Story online classes\; admission to the Writing C
 ircle\; a USD 2\,000 stipend and free admission to the week-long summer wr
 iters' conference with craft lectures\, an intensive fiction workshop and 
 panels with literary agents and publishers\; and a full manuscript review 
 and consultation with executive editor Hannah Tinti (story collection or n
 ovel in progress up to 150 pages / 35\,000 words). ELIGIBILITY: early-care
 er fiction writers who have not yet published a book\, have never been enr
 olled in an advanced degree programme (MA or MFA) in creative writing\, En
 glish or literature and have no plans to attend one in 2027\, and are at l
 east 21 years old as of 1 January 2027. Applicants outside the United Stat
 es are welcome. The fellowship seeks writing that centres\, celebrates or 
 reclaims being marginalised through the lens of race\, ethnicity\, gender\
 , sexuality\, age\, class\, religion\, illness\, disability\, trauma\, mig
 ration\, displacement\, dispossession or imprisonment. APPLY via Submittab
 le with a fiction sample of 3\,000 to 5\,000 words (multiple stories allow
 ed within the limit\, one file)\, a personal statement of 400 to 750 words
 \, a statement of purpose of 200 to 350 words\, two references (contact de
 tails only\, no letters) and a current resume including writing classes\, 
 awards\, publications and residencies. Applications open 8 September and c
 lose 13 October 2026 at 23:59 ET\; the winner is announced in January 2027
 .\n\nOrganisation: One Story (with the Talve-Goodman Family)\nLocation: Re
 mote year-long mentorship with One Story magazine (Brooklyn\, US)\; includ
 es free admission to the week-long summer writers' conference. Open to app
 licants outside the United States.\nAward: USD 2\,000 stipend plus free ad
 mission to One Story's week-long summer writers' conference\, access to On
 e Story online classes\, admission to the Writing Circle\, and a full manu
 script review and consultation with Executive Editor Hannah Tinti (story c
 ollection or novel in progress up to 150 pages / 35\,000 words). No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Year-long fellowship for 2027. Applications open 8 S
 eptember 2026 and close 13 October 2026 at 23:59 ET\; winner announced pub
 licly in January 2027.\n\nMore: https://one-story.com/learn/fellowship/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://one-story.com/learn/fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote year-long mentorship with One Story magazine (Brooklyn\, US
 )\; includes free admission to the week-long summer writers' conference. O
 pen to applicants outside the United States.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pedantic-arts-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Arts Residency (Pittsburgh): visual artist\, cur
 ator and writer cohort
DESCRIPTION:The Pedantic Arts Residency re-embraces the impact that educati
 on\, study and structured contemplation can have on artistic output by int
 erconnecting creators\, organizers and critics: each four-week cohort brin
 gs together three creatives\, one practicing visual art\, one curating\, a
 nd one writing\, for exchange and cross-disciplinary dialogue. Each reside
 nt receives a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment on Penn Avenue in one
  of Pittsburgh's largest art hubs\, a USD 2\,000 honorarium to use at thei
 r discretion (half on arrival\, half on completion)\, help establishing co
 nnections relevant to their research goals\, and a Pittsburgh-based guide 
 working in a similar field. Weekly programming includes private dinners\, 
 studio visits and museum tours\, some open to the public and some reserved
  for the cohort. No final deliverable is required\; Pedantic prioritizes i
 mmersion over production\, though living at the apartment for the full pro
 gram is required. ELIGIBILITY: creatives aged 18+ living outside the great
 er Pittsburgh metropolitan area (Pittsburgh-based creatives are not eligib
 le). APPLICATION: submission requirements vary by role (images for visual 
 artists\, writing samples for writers\, documentation for organizers)\, as
  PDF or ZIP files\; submit by 15 October for the upcoming cohort. Cohorts 
 run each January and June.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts\nLocation: Pitts
 burgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). Only for creatives
  living outside the greater Pittsburgh metro area (Allegheny\, Armstrong\,
  Beaver\, Butler\, Fayette\, Washington and Westmoreland counties)\; appli
 cants must be 18 or older.\nAward: USD 2\,000 honorarium per resident (hal
 f on arrival\, half on completion)\, plus a free private bedroom in a furn
 ished three-bedroom apartment\, a Pittsburgh-based guide in a similar fiel
 d\, and weekly programming (private dinners\, studio visits\, museum tours
 ). No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: Four weeks\; cohorts run twice
  a year\, in January and June.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.org/residency
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). Only 
 for creatives living outside the greater Pittsburgh metro area (Allegheny\
 , Armstrong\, Beaver\, Butler\, Fayette\, Washington and Westmoreland coun
 ties)\; applicants must be 18 or older.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pedantic-research-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pedantic Research Grant (Pittsburgh): one to two week res
 earch stays
DESCRIPTION:The Pedantic Research Grant is a derivative program of the Peda
 ntic Arts Residency offering another way to be immersed in Pittsburgh's co
 mmunities: an independent opportunity for visual artists\, curators and wr
 iters to conduct self-motivated\, Pittsburgh-related research. The stay ru
 ns one or two weeks\, scheduled flexibly between the grantee and the Pedan
 tic Crew\, and is based on Penn Avenue in one of Pittsburgh's largest art 
 hubs. The grantee receives a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment\, an h
 onorarium of USD 500 or USD 1\,000 depending on length\, and help establis
 hing connections to individuals and organizations key to the research goal
 s. ELIGIBILITY: past Pedantic Arts Residency participants continuing to de
 velop their experiences\, or new candidates with a uniquely specific reaso
 n to be in Pittsburgh. APPLICATION: submit via the Open Call by 15 October
  for the upcoming cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Pedantic Arts\nLocation: Pittsbu
 rgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For visual artists\,
  curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pittsburgh-related
  research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency participants.\nAward
 : USD 500 (one week) or USD 1\,000 (two weeks) honorarium to use at the gr
 antee's discretion\, plus a free bedroom at the Pedantic Apartment and ass
 istance establishing connections relevant to the research goals. No applic
 ation fee mentioned.\nDuration: One or two weeks\, scheduled at the discre
 tion of the grantee and the Pedantic Crew.\n\nMore: https://pedanticarts.o
 rg/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://pedanticarts.org/research-grant/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Pittsburgh\, Pennsylvania\, USA (Penn Avenue arts corridor). For v
 isual artists\, curators and writers with a specific reason to conduct Pit
 tsburgh-related research\; also open to past Pedantic Arts Residency parti
 cipants.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vermont-studio-center-open-call-jul-dec-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T212827Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Vermont Studio Center: Residency Open Call for July to De
 cember 2027
DESCRIPTION:A Vermont Studio Center residency provides artists and writers 
 from around the world with time and space to deepen their creative practic
 e while building a network of mentors\, collaborators and friends. Session
 s run two\, three or four weeks and include resident presentations\, open 
 studios\, and the acclaimed Visiting Artists and Writers program. Applicat
 ions are juried in a single pool by a rotating jury of practicing artists 
 and writers\, and each deadline carries fellowship opportunities listed on
  the fellowships page. FUNDING: VSC awards full fellowships to 35 percent 
 of residents and partial fellowships to all accepted applicants\; partial 
 fellows pay USD 2\,700 for two weeks\, USD 3\,825 for three weeks or USD 4
 \,950 for four weeks (10 percent off when sharing a bathroom with one othe
 r resident\, subject to availability). Applicants whose work is well recei
 ved but not awarded a named fellowship may still be invited for admission.
  NOTE: unless you win a full fellowship\, attending carries a significant 
 fee\, so weigh this one against fully funded options. KEY DATES: this open
  call closes 30 September 2026 at 11:59PM EST and fills residencies from J
 uly to December 2027\; the next cycle runs 15 February to 31 March\, and V
 T Week applications run 15 December to 31 January.\n\nOrganisation: Vermon
 t Studio Center\nLocation: Johnson\, Vermont\, USA. Open to artists and wr
 iters from around the world.\nAward: Every accepted resident receives at l
 east a partial fellowship\; 35 percent of residents receive full fellowshi
 ps covering the residency. Partial fellows pay a program fee of USD 2\,700
  (two weeks)\, USD 3\,825 (three weeks) or USD 4\,950 (four weeks)\, with 
 a 10 percent discount for sharing a bathroom. Application fee not stated o
 n the call page.\nDuration: Two\, three or four week sessions between July
  and December 2027.\n\nMore: https://vermontstudiocenter.org/apply?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://vermontstudiocenter.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Johnson\, Vermont\, USA. Open to artists and writers from around t
 he world.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
